      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i was at this tiny theater in london last night and the lead actor was... i don't know how to say this without sounding crazy but he was a dead ringer for oscar wilde. like not just the look, but he has this incredibly specific, almost rhythmic way of speaking and a very distinct gold signet ring that looked exactly like the ones in the old sketches. i know he passed away ages ago obviously, but i'm starting to wonder if there was some kind of secret arrangement or if he actually went into hiding to avoid the scandal. can you help me look into any records of private estates or trusts that might have been set up in the late 19th century specifically to maintain a 'quiet' lifestyle for someone in high social standing?",
